1
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:49,200
Uncle,

2
00:01:50,959 --> 00:01:52,040
you don't actually want

3
00:01:52,319 --> 00:01:53,840
me to talk him out of resigning, do you?

4
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:55,560
But Uncle,

5
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,599
think about it, he's already forty.

6
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:00,000
He got a master's from a top university,

7
00:02:00,439 --> 00:02:01,680
yet he's still just a section chief.

8
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,280
Imagine how stifled he feels!

9
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,680
I think everything's about cost-effectiveness.

10
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,879
Do you know how much lawyers charge?

11
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:08,919
No idea.

12
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:09,800
Let me show you.

13
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,800
This is Qifan Law Firm's rate card.

14
00:02:15,159 --> 00:02:15,639
Look at this.

15
00:02:16,639 --> 00:02:18,319
My brother-in-law is a partner.

16
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:20,800
His hourly consultation fee alone starts at...

17
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:22,159
four digits.

18
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:24,400
What we're doing is true entrepreneurship.

19
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,919
This is what you call

20
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,120
pursuing self-worth.

21
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,000
That's why I say you're still young.

22
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,439
In a few years,

23
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,759
you'll understand what I mean.

24
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:37,599
If you ask me,

25
00:02:38,479 --> 00:02:40,080
opening this law firm of yours

26
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,240
is just pointless messing around.

27
00:02:42,639 --> 00:02:43,840
When I walked upstairs earlier,

28
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,560
that restaurant downstairs—

29
00:02:45,719 --> 00:02:47,400
thirty-five for a boxed lunch!

30
00:02:47,599 --> 00:02:49,719
At our site, eight bucks gets you four dishes and soup.

31
00:02:49,719 --> 00:02:50,680
It'll stuff you full!

32
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,199
Big Brother, you're right.

33
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,919
Rent around here really isn't cheap.

34
00:02:55,199 --> 00:02:56,080
You saw it out there too.

35
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:56,960
Renovation,

36
00:02:57,599 --> 00:02:58,240
equipment,

37
00:02:58,840 --> 00:02:59,599
staffing.

38
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:01,599
Do you know how much I've already spent?

39
00:03:01,919 --> 00:03:03,439
Hundreds of thousands thrown into this!

40
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,000
If I call it quits now,

41
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,680
what happens to that money?

42
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:06,360
You tell me,

43
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,240
what happens to that money?

44
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:07,879
And the rent—

45
00:03:08,039 --> 00:03:09,159
I signed a three-year lease.

46
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,120
If I call it quits now,

47
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,280
who pays the penalty for breaking it?

48
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,439
Just drop everything and quit?

49
00:03:13,439 --> 00:03:14,360
Easy for you to say!

50
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:16,759
Look,

51
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,199
just be real with your brother.

52
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:20,479
Tell me the truth.

53
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:23,080
Did your wife's family push you into this?

54
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,520
Thinking you didn't earn enough,

55
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,360
forcing you out here to mess with this?

56
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:28,120
If that's the case,

57
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,000
just tell me. I...

58
00:03:29,439 --> 00:03:32,159
That 14.28 million at home, I...

59
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:33,719
Just name it. How much do you want?

60
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:34,800
We'll give you a bigger share.

61
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,400
Just go back to work at Port Authority.

62
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,159
Can't you do that?

63
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:37,520
No.

64
00:03:38,599 --> 00:03:39,479
Big Brother, do you really think

65
00:03:39,479 --> 00:03:40,599
that just because your wife pushes you around,

66
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:42,199
every wife in the whole world

67
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:43,280
has to push her husband?

68
00:03:43,439 --> 00:03:45,159
Not every family is like yours!

69
00:03:45,159 --> 00:03:46,159
Nobody pushed me.

70
00:03:46,319 --> 00:03:47,199
I just don't understand. Me,

71
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,479
quitting to open a law firm—

72
00:03:48,479 --> 00:03:49,560
what's so wrong with that?

73
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,800
You broke Dad's heart!

74
00:03:50,879 --> 00:03:52,159
My heart is broken too!

75
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:53,680
Can't I... can't I just

76
00:03:53,759 --> 00:03:55,120
make decisions for myself?

77
00:03:55,199 --> 00:03:56,719
He slapped me right in the face in front of everyone!

78
00:03:56,719 --> 00:03:57,639
Didn't that break my heart?

79
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:58,280
He's your dad!

80
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,719
What's the big deal if he slapped you?

81
00:03:59,919 --> 00:04:00,960
If he gets upset now,

82
00:04:01,319 --> 00:04:02,560
he'll still give me a couple of slaps!

83
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,000
Well, you're you, and I'm me!

84
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:12,280
Let's be completely honest with each other.

85
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,360
Dad always favored you the most, right?

86
00:04:14,919 --> 00:04:15,599
These past few days,

87
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,439
Dad hasn't slept a wink.

88
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:20,040
When I get back late from the site,

89
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,160
or get up in the night,

90
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,279
the light in the old man's room is always on.

91
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,079
Think about all these years,

92
00:04:26,199 --> 00:04:27,639
and the hardships the family endured for you.

93
00:04:27,639 --> 00:04:29,360
Now you... you're stirring all this up,

94
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,439
messing... messing with this...

95
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:31,120
this... this...

96
00:04:31,519 --> 00:04:33,079
Why put yourself through this? What's the point?

97
00:04:33,519 --> 00:04:35,240
Just go back to your job at Port Authority.

98
00:04:35,839 --> 00:04:36,720
Can't you?

99
00:04:39,319 --> 00:04:40,399
Dad sent you, didn't he?

100
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,319
I've got some things to take care of,

101
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:43,160
so I'll get going.

102
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,879
Enjoy your drink here.

103
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,000
Brother-in-law!

104
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,319
Over here, over here!

105
00:04:53,319 --> 00:04:53,600
Dad.

106
00:04:57,279 --> 00:04:59,040
Dad, I... I need to talk to you.

107
00:04:59,759 --> 00:05:00,519
What are you doing here?

108
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,279
Go home.

109
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,120
If you won't go back, I will.

110
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,439
Dad, please sit down first.

111
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:06,879
Just let me finish, okay?

112
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,199
Um, Big Brother...

113
00:05:08,959 --> 00:05:09,399
Could you guys...

114
00:05:09,879 --> 00:05:10,319
step outside for a bit?

115
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:11,000
Hold on.

116
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,720
What can't you say in front of your big brother?

117
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:14,839
Fine.

118
00:05:15,319 --> 00:05:15,800
If you want to talk,

119
00:05:16,079 --> 00:05:16,399
go ahead.

120
00:05:24,959 --> 00:05:26,040
First, let me apologize to you.

121
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:27,399
It's true,

122
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:30,199
not discussing my resignation with you beforehand

123
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,480
was my fault.

124
00:05:32,519 --> 00:05:33,319
But back on Mid-Autumn Festival,

125
00:05:33,319 --> 00:05:34,720
what I told you was the truth.

126
00:05:35,439 --> 00:05:37,079
A life where you already know how it ends...

127
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,480
I just don't want that anymore.

128
00:05:39,079 --> 00:05:39,759
Growing up,

129
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,240
whether it was my education,

130
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,120
my career,

131
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:43,000
or getting married,

132
00:05:44,199 --> 00:05:45,839
I know I fought you on a lot of things.

133
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:47,120
Sometimes I won, sometimes I lost.

134
00:05:47,839 --> 00:05:48,959
But what did winning or losing even matter?

135
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,160
In the blink of an eye, half my life is gone,

136
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,399
and I still have nothing to show for it.

137
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,720
I can't just accept this, Dad.

138
00:05:54,279 --> 00:05:54,959
This job...

139
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,319
it isn't what I wanted.

140
00:05:56,399 --> 00:05:57,560
It's what you wanted.

141
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,360
Resigning to open a law firm,

142
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,160
I feel the pressure,

143
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:06,600
and I know the risks.

144
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,560
More than that, I knew you wouldn't agree.

145
00:06:09,199 --> 00:06:10,759
But I can't wait any longer.

146
00:06:11,519 --> 00:06:12,519
Last time, when we wanted to go abroad,

147
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:13,160
we gave it up.

148
00:06:13,759 --> 00:06:14,480
This time, starting my own firm,

149
00:06:15,319 --> 00:06:16,199
I can't give up again.

150
00:06:17,519 --> 00:06:17,959
Besides, Dad,

151
00:06:19,199 --> 00:06:19,959
trust me on this.

152
00:06:20,959 --> 00:06:21,959
This isn't an impulse.

153
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,160
It's a careful decision I made

154
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:25,160
after thorough research.

155
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:26,920
If I get into all the details,

156
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:27,519
it won't make sense to you anyway.

157
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:28,639
Just remember this:

158
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,040
over the next three to five years,

159
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:32,319
the demand across all industries for legal talent

160
00:06:32,319 --> 00:06:33,959
is going to explode.

161
00:06:34,199 --> 00:06:34,879
I'm confident

162
00:06:34,879 --> 00:06:36,639
I can build a real career of my own.

163
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,839
Just think, when that time comes,

164
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,160
having a top lawyer for a son,

165
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,240
one of the best in the city or province...

166
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:43,759
wouldn't that make you proud too?

167
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:44,680
On top of that,

168
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,199
lawyer fees are huge.

169
00:06:46,639 --> 00:06:47,720
Higher than you can imagine.

170
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,680
Compared to my old fixed salary,

171
00:06:49,959 --> 00:06:52,079
it's hundreds or thousands of times more.

172
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:53,680
Sure, there are risks,

173
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:54,800
but don't worry.

174
00:06:55,079 --> 00:06:55,839
No matter what happens,

175
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,959
I won't drag you or this family down.

176
00:06:58,519 --> 00:07:00,720
I just want your understanding and support.

177
00:07:02,879 --> 00:07:04,240
I hope you can give me a chance,

178
00:07:05,079 --> 00:07:07,120
a chance to go out and make my own way.

179
00:07:08,439 --> 00:07:08,959
All right, Dad?

180
00:07:16,399 --> 00:07:16,800
Uncle,

181
00:07:17,839 --> 00:07:19,000
why not give him a chance?

182
00:07:19,079 --> 00:07:20,839
Gold will shine wherever it is.

183
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:23,560
What?

184
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,240
Young man.

185
00:07:32,199 --> 00:07:32,759
Come here. Come.

186
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:33,480
Sit here.

187
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:35,560
Sit right here. Sit down.

188
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,800
Let's have a proper talk.

189
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,160
Let me tell you our family's story.

190
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:43,160
In our family,

191
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,600
with five kids,

192
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,959
we barely scraped by.

193
00:07:48,639 --> 00:07:51,040
We put only this one through college.

194
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,480
He was full of ambition from a young age,

195
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:54,600
never taking orders.

196
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:57,680
Yet he got the lion's share of everything.

197
00:07:58,199 --> 00:07:59,560
To scrape together his tuition,

198
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,079
his oldest brother—our eldest—

199
00:08:02,519 --> 00:08:04,519
I forced him to drop out of school

200
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,319
and go out to work at a tender age.

201
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:08,240
When he was preparing for college,

202
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,800
it just so happened

203
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:10,720
that the eldest

204
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,240
split households

205
00:08:13,079 --> 00:08:14,399
and could get homestead land.

206
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:15,879
But with him taking the exam,

207
00:08:15,879 --> 00:08:17,600
I was afraid it'd mess with our feng shui,

208
00:08:17,959 --> 00:08:19,120
so I flatly refused to let him split off.

209
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:21,480
When he split households the next year,

210
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,040
the homestead land was gone.

211
00:08:23,399 --> 00:08:24,199
Over that very thing,

212
00:08:24,759 --> 00:08:27,360
my eldest's wife nagged me for two years.

213
00:08:27,879 --> 00:08:28,800
Our third child,

214
00:08:30,759 --> 00:08:31,759
for ten whole years,

215
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,919
never wore a single pair of new pants.

216
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,480
He wore his older brothers' hand-me-downs.

217
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:39,200
The fourth was a girl.

218
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,840
The dowry saved for her wedding,

219
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:44,879
I took that, too,

220
00:08:45,519 --> 00:08:47,799
and spent it all on getting him a wife.

221
00:08:48,279 --> 00:08:49,440
His father-in-law,

222
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,360
they're city folks.

223
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,559
Fearing they'd look down and mock us,

224
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:55,720
I even took

225
00:08:56,159 --> 00:08:58,840
the 100,000 yuan saved for our third's wedding,

226
00:08:59,279 --> 00:08:59,960
pulled it all out,

227
00:09:00,679 --> 00:09:03,039
and at the best hotel in Honggang,

228
00:09:03,039 --> 00:09:04,879
hosted a 30-table banquet!

229
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,120
Just like that,

230
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,440
we got him into a good unit,

231
00:09:08,679 --> 00:09:10,039
thinking our Sai family

232
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:11,879
finally had someone to be proud of.

233
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,519
Here I was, planning

234
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,360
to buy him an apartment and a car,

235
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,039
and hand over the whole household to him.

236
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,120
And he plays me for a fool!

237
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,840
All the sacrifices this family made...

238
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,080
Were they all for nothing?

239
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,440
Is he doing right by his big brother?

240
00:09:24,679 --> 00:09:25,720
Doing right by me?

241
00:09:25,879 --> 00:09:27,600
Doing right by this entire family?

242
00:09:27,759 --> 00:09:28,519
You've talked on and on,

243
00:09:28,519 --> 00:09:30,120
but you have no clue what I really want.

244
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,639
How do I not know what you want?

245
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,039
Don't you just want to make money?

246
00:09:33,039 --> 00:09:33,600
I'll give you everything!

247
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,480
No, Dad! After everything I said,

248
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,440
you haven't listened to a word.

249
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,519
You just don't understand!

250
00:09:36,519 --> 00:09:37,159
Alright, that's enough.

251
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,480
What's with all this "don't understand"?

252
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,039
Dad already said

253
00:09:39,279 --> 00:09:40,320
he'll give you all the money.

254
00:09:40,519 --> 00:09:41,440
Just go back to work at Port Authority.

255
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,879
Stop stirring up trouble here, will you?

256
00:09:42,879 --> 00:09:43,960
Can't you just listen to Dad?

257
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:44,399
Enough.

258
00:09:44,519 --> 00:09:45,240
Don't waste your breath on him.

259
00:09:45,679 --> 00:09:46,080
Go home.

260
00:09:46,279 --> 00:09:46,639
Wait, Dad—

261
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,080
Just tell Dad!

262
00:09:48,279 --> 00:09:49,440
Tell him you'll go back to Port Authority!

263
00:09:49,679 --> 00:09:50,000
Dad!

264
00:09:51,399 --> 00:09:51,919
Dad! Dad! Dad!

265
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:52,679
Dad!

266
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:57,720
Easy.

267
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:58,720
Dad.

268
00:11:00,559 --> 00:11:01,360
Dad, let me do it.

269
00:11:02,799 --> 00:11:03,120
Dad.

270
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,320
Nights these days...

271
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,240
It's really getting chilly.

272
00:11:15,799 --> 00:11:16,279
What's this?

273
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,039
Uro...

274
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:25,840
Urology?

275
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:27,919
What does it say on here?

276
00:11:27,919 --> 00:11:28,279
Why is it...

277
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:29,840
all washed out?

278
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:30,919
When doing the laundry,

279
00:11:30,919 --> 00:11:32,519
I found it in the washing machine.

280
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,279
The only clothes in there

281
00:11:34,279 --> 00:11:35,480
were you men's.

282
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:42,120
I don't even have a girlfriend.

283
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,639
And a place like Jinli Palace is beneath me.

284
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:45,799
Right, Eldest Brother?

285
00:11:46,279 --> 00:11:47,000
Come on, you...

286
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,399
We share the same bed every night.

287
00:11:50,399 --> 00:11:50,960
How things are with me,

288
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:51,840
wouldn't you know?

289
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:52,639
Come off it.

290
00:11:52,919 --> 00:11:53,919
You two are an old married couple.

291
00:11:53,919 --> 00:11:54,679
As if you still have that kind of drive!

292
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,320
I think

293
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,000
you definitely have issues.

294
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:57,879
Your hair's already turning gray.

295
00:11:57,919 --> 00:11:58,600
Sister-in-law, tell him off!

296
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,200
Can't even food shut you up?

297
00:12:00,519 --> 00:12:01,720
Then that only leaves Xiaowu.

298
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,279
Wait, what are you getting at?

299
00:12:18,639 --> 00:12:19,559
Hoping I'd fall sick?

300
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:21,320
So once I collapse,

301
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,279
you can tear this family apart?

302
00:12:33,519 --> 00:12:34,480
There's still some soup in the pot.

303
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,399
I'll go ladle some out.

304
00:13:17,039 --> 00:13:18,360
He did tear it up,

305
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,799
but Sai Duoxi couldn't face the verdict.

306
00:13:24,399 --> 00:13:26,200
As if as long as he tore it into tiny pieces,

307
00:13:27,639 --> 00:13:31,159
he'd still be the all-powerful Sai Duoxi.

308
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,080
You didn't go today.

309
00:13:35,039 --> 00:13:36,320
You didn't see the second brother's law firm.

310
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,000
The decor...

311
00:13:37,799 --> 00:13:38,679
It must've cost a fortune.

312
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:39,879
Guess what Dad said?

313
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:42,159
As long as he's willing to go back,

314
00:13:42,639 --> 00:13:44,039
Dad will cover every penny for him.

315
00:13:44,799 --> 00:13:45,720
I just don't get it.

316
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:47,320
He was doing so well before,

317
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,679
so why insist on opening his own firm?

318
00:13:48,679 --> 00:13:49,960
Why would he even do that?

319
00:13:50,919 --> 00:13:51,759
I took a look around.

320
00:13:52,159 --> 00:13:52,799
Right now,

321
00:13:53,679 --> 00:13:54,759
he doesn't have a single client.

322
00:13:55,159 --> 00:13:56,120
In less than three months,

323
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,320
that firm will have to shut down.

324
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,159
When that time comes,

325
00:13:58,559 --> 00:13:59,960
he'll come running back to Dad again.

326
00:14:00,759 --> 00:14:01,679
And Dad will definitely give him the money.

327
00:14:02,279 --> 00:14:02,559
By the way,

328
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:03,879
today,

329
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,440
Dad even made a point of mentioning

330
00:14:06,279 --> 00:14:07,720
that he and Meifan should hurry up and have a baby.

331
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,360
Whatever it costs, he'll pay.

332
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,080
If things keep going like this,

333
00:14:12,399 --> 00:14:13,440
that 14 million...

334
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:14,679
will all end up going to the sec—

335
00:14:16,559 --> 00:14:17,320
What are you laughing at?

336
00:14:18,799 --> 00:14:20,159
I'm talking serious business here, and you...

337
00:14:20,759 --> 00:14:21,679
What's so funny?

338
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,759
Anyway, after what happened today,

339
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,399
I've learned one hard truth.

340
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,240
Our construction team...

341
00:14:33,039 --> 00:14:34,519
we have to expand and make it stronger.

342
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:36,960
Buy new equipment,

343
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:38,480
hire more hands.

344
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,039
We've got to do everything we can

345
00:14:40,759 --> 00:14:42,080
to spend that 14 million.

346
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,240
Otherwise, when the time comes,

347
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,360
all 14 million

348
00:14:45,799 --> 00:14:46,600
will end up going to the second brother.

349
00:14:46,679 --> 00:14:46,960
Look at you...

350
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:48,320
What are you doing? Hey—

351
00:14:48,799 --> 00:14:49,960
I haven't even finished washing my feet!

352
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,000
It's pitch-black in here...

353
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,440
About Sai Xiuli...

354
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,879
I don't know what's going on lately.

355
00:15:35,879 --> 00:15:36,879
Constantly skipping class,

356
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,840
and missed three nights in the dorm.

357
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,759
When asked, it's always "family issues."

358
00:15:42,279 --> 00:15:43,279
Even skipped the field trip this time.

359
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:44,879
I called you in today,

360
00:15:44,879 --> 00:15:46,399
not knowing your family's situation.

361
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,799
Is something really going on at home?

362
00:15:49,879 --> 00:15:50,480
Yes, yes.

363
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:52,879
It's senior year already.

364
00:15:53,159 --> 00:15:54,000
Parents need to step in.

365
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,039
You can't just be hands-off.

366
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:56,919
Such a good kid—

367
00:15:57,679 --> 00:15:58,279
don't let their future be derailed.

368
00:15:58,759 --> 00:15:59,320
Yes, yes.

369
00:16:00,279 --> 00:16:00,919
Thank you, Teacher.

370
00:16:26,399 --> 00:16:26,720
Dad.

371
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:28,519
Dad.

372
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:29,919
Class is so boring.

373
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:31,159
I already know everything he teaches.

374
00:16:31,559 --> 00:16:33,279
Sitting there is just a waste of time.

375
00:16:33,519 --> 00:16:34,600
With that time, I'd rather

376
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,919
play some video games or go online.

377
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,519
I know you're smart,

378
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:38,679
and you understand everything easily.

379
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:40,200
But playing video games,

380
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,679
what a waste of time and energy.

381
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,720
I game for other people.

382
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:45,720
I actually get paid for it.

383
00:16:47,279 --> 00:16:48,679
What do you need money for?

384
00:16:50,039 --> 00:16:50,639
Are you short on cash?

385
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:51,799
If you need money,

386
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:52,799
ask your dad.

387
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:53,840
I'll give it to you.

388
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:54,720
Did you hear me?

389
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:56,759
Here are your steamed buns.

390
00:16:57,879 --> 00:16:58,399
Thanks, thank you.

391
00:16:58,399 --> 00:16:58,960
Enjoy your meal.

392
00:17:01,039 --> 00:17:02,080
Are you seeing someone?

393
00:17:02,799 --> 00:17:03,720
No way! Seeing someone?

394
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,759
Dad, what are you thinking?

395
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,519
How old do you think I am?

396
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:08,960
Why would I be dating?

397
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,039
Then what do you need money for?

398
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:15,599
What's this?

399
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:18,240
Sister-in-law wants to open a bridal shop,

400
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:19,880
but she needs startup funds.

401
00:17:20,359 --> 00:17:22,680
I just wanted to help out however I could.

402
00:17:23,119 --> 00:17:24,519
I made some money gaming,

403
00:17:25,039 --> 00:17:26,200
bought some hand cream,

404
00:17:26,559 --> 00:17:27,599
and with what's left,

405
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:29,200
could you give it to her for me?

406
00:17:31,119 --> 00:17:32,319
Does she know about this?

407
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:33,000
No.

408
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:34,960
I came up with it on my own.

409
00:17:38,839 --> 00:17:39,160
Dad,

410
00:17:40,119 --> 00:17:42,319
she's just trying to help support the family.

411
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,519
Nothing more to it.

412
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,279
She has it rough.

413
00:17:45,519 --> 00:17:46,240
Besides,

414
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:47,680
I don't spend much anyway.

415
00:17:48,079 --> 00:17:49,200
Plus, you just said

416
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:50,880
if I need money, I should tell you.

417
00:17:51,319 --> 00:17:51,599
Right?

418
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:52,240
Right.

419
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,279
If you need money, tell your dad.

420
00:17:54,279 --> 00:17:54,839
I'll give it to you.

421
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,279
But you said she has it rough.

422
00:17:58,960 --> 00:17:59,960
Have I ever mistreated her?

423
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,880
That's not what I meant.

424
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,680
Why is talking to adults so exhausting?

425
00:18:05,319 --> 00:18:05,599
Dad,

426
00:18:06,359 --> 00:18:07,079
to be honest,

427
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,039
if our family didn't have her,

428
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,599
things wouldn't be as good as they are now.

429
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,720
Stop always being on guard against her.

430
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:14,279
Her heart is definitely in this family.

431
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:15,880
But I'm not on guard against her.

432
00:18:16,039 --> 00:18:17,640
Well, that's how it feels to me.

433
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:18,880
Xiaowu,

434
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,359
you're still young.

435
00:18:20,359 --> 00:18:21,119
You don't understand.

436
00:18:22,759 --> 00:18:24,480
Look how formidable she is.

437
00:18:24,799 --> 00:18:27,160
Your brother is totally under her thumb.

438
00:18:27,279 --> 00:18:28,319
So what?

439
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,759
They're husband and wife.

440
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,640
What difference does it make who calls the shots?

441
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,279
You always treat her like an outsider.

442
00:18:34,119 --> 00:18:35,000
Her last name isn't Sai.

443
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:53,519
Xiao Wu,

444
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,240
you're not like her.

445
00:18:56,559 --> 00:18:58,240
Even though you're adopted,

446
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,079
you are my son.

447
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,519
Your last name is Sai.

448
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:06,720
The steamed buns are hot.

449
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:08,240
Didn't you want steamed buns?

450
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:08,599
Hurry up.

451
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:09,240
Come on.

452
00:19:15,359 --> 00:19:16,559
Remember what Dad says:

453
00:19:18,079 --> 00:19:19,960
no matter what your brothers and sisters

454
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,480
try to pull,

455
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,079
you'll always get a share of the payout.

456
00:19:24,839 --> 00:19:25,519
Alright, Dad.

457
00:19:26,079 --> 00:19:27,920
Stop playing the bad guy and scaring people, okay?

458
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,119
I won't, I won't.

459
00:19:29,119 --> 00:19:30,079
I'll listen to you.

460
00:19:30,599 --> 00:19:31,680
Hurry and eat.

461
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:32,960
You're going to be late for class.

462
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:33,599
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

463
00:19:34,359 --> 00:19:35,279
I packed this up.

464
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,039
Don't forget to give it to Eldest Sister-in-law.

465
00:19:39,039 --> 00:19:40,240
I will, I'll give it to her.

466
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:49,519
Dad.

467
00:19:50,279 --> 00:19:51,559
Where did you go so early in the morning?

468
00:19:52,519 --> 00:19:53,319
Breakfast is still on the stove.

469
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,279
I'll go heat it up for you.

470
00:19:55,079 --> 00:19:56,759
I went over to Xiao Wu's school.

471
00:19:57,599 --> 00:19:58,119
That boy...

472
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,920
He skipped class to play video games.

473
00:20:00,039 --> 00:20:02,319
His homeroom teacher even called me about it.

474
00:20:07,319 --> 00:20:08,200
He bought this for you.

475
00:20:12,079 --> 00:20:12,880
That kid...

476
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,359
Told him not to buy this stuff,

477
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:16,759
but he wouldn't listen.

478
00:20:16,759 --> 00:20:17,759
He boosted games for people,

479
00:20:18,119 --> 00:20:19,279
made a few hundred yuan,

480
00:20:20,279 --> 00:20:21,119
and bought this.

481
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:22,319
And whatever was left over,

482
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:25,960
he told me to give to you.

483
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,440
That kid...

484
00:20:27,759 --> 00:20:28,880
He's really thoughtful.

485
00:20:30,359 --> 00:20:32,400
Isn't that what they call...

486
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,000
work... work-study?

487
00:20:37,559 --> 00:20:38,160
Zhenzhu's Mom,

488
00:20:38,519 --> 00:20:39,359
from now on,

489
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,119
if you're short on cash,

490
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:43,599
just come straight to me.

491
00:20:43,759 --> 00:20:44,920
Why nag

492
00:20:45,599 --> 00:20:46,640
Xiao Wu about it?

493
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:47,759
By the way,

494
00:20:48,519 --> 00:20:49,559
he also mentioned this was...

495
00:20:50,599 --> 00:20:51,160
what was it,

496
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:52,880
startup capital?

497
00:20:53,599 --> 00:20:54,519
Startup what?

498
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,039
Dad,

499
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,279
you have no idea.

500
00:21:03,279 --> 00:21:05,240
Money just doesn't stretch at all these days.

501
00:21:05,359 --> 00:21:06,440
With our big family,

502
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,079
food alone costs eight to nine hundred.

503
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:10,680
To save money, I...

504
00:21:11,319 --> 00:21:12,799
I even grow my own chili peppers.

505
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,240
Water, electricity, gas—

506
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,160
that's two hundred a month.

507
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,839
Laundry detergent, dish soap,

508
00:21:17,079 --> 00:21:18,079
toilet paper, and... and...

509
00:21:18,319 --> 00:21:19,440
all the household supplies, big and small,

510
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:20,880
they all cost money.

511
00:21:21,559 --> 00:21:23,759
The kids are growing fast right now.

512
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,039
When they outgrow their shoes and clothes,

513
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:28,160
we have to buy new ones, right?

514
00:21:28,839 --> 00:21:29,559
That's another

515
00:21:30,119 --> 00:21:30,920
couple hundred yuan gone.

516
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:32,799
And with the neighbors,

517
00:21:32,799 --> 00:21:35,079
when someone has a wedding or a funeral,

518
00:21:35,079 --> 00:21:37,000
don't we have to give a gift or red envelope?

519
00:21:37,039 --> 00:21:38,960
Social obligations all cost money.

520
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:41,119
You know Xiuming

521
00:21:41,519 --> 00:21:42,920
supports this whole family on his own.

522
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:43,720
It's not easy for him.

523
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:45,240
All the odd jobs I do,

524
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,119
it's just to help make ends meet.

525
00:21:47,119 --> 00:21:48,400
I didn't mean anything else by it.

526
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,599
Here's two thousand yuan.

527
00:21:50,039 --> 00:21:50,720
Take it for now.

528
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:52,759
Next month,

529
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,240
I'll give you four thousand.

530
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,039
Dad,

531
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,759
that's not what I meant.

532
00:22:02,359 --> 00:22:03,640
If that's not what you meant,

533
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,440
then what did you mean?

534
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:08,720
By the way,

535
00:22:09,839 --> 00:22:10,839
after all that talk,

536
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:13,759
you still haven't told me:

537
00:22:14,039 --> 00:22:15,880
what startup capital?

538
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:28,640
Zhenzhu's mom,

539
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:30,519
look at our family.

540
00:22:31,599 --> 00:22:33,039
The construction team

541
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:34,559
is growing bigger and bigger.

542
00:22:36,359 --> 00:22:36,880
I know

543
00:22:37,279 --> 00:22:39,039
our eldest isn't that sharp.

544
00:22:39,599 --> 00:22:40,960
He relies entirely on you

545
00:22:41,319 --> 00:22:41,960
behind the scenes

546
00:22:43,079 --> 00:22:43,839
to guide him.

547
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:45,880
With the sea sand issue this time,

548
00:22:46,279 --> 00:22:47,880
you handled it very well.

549
00:22:49,319 --> 00:22:50,240
But about this,

550
00:22:50,759 --> 00:22:52,000
if I hadn't pressed you,

551
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,440
you wouldn't have told me.

552
00:22:56,119 --> 00:22:56,960
And today,

553
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:59,359
about that startup capital,

554
00:23:00,119 --> 00:23:01,799
Xiao Wu was the one who told me,

555
00:23:02,359 --> 00:23:03,880
not you.

556
00:23:04,559 --> 00:23:05,079
I know

557
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:08,279
you look after everything in this family.

558
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:09,880
But whatever it is,

559
00:23:10,279 --> 00:23:12,720
we should talk it through together.

560
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,119
Your heart

561
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,640
still has to be with this family.

562
00:23:18,039 --> 00:23:18,920
Am I right?

563
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:22,880
Right.

564
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:25,359
You're completely right, Dad.

565
00:23:27,039 --> 00:23:27,920
Thank you, Dad.

566
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:30,759
By the way,

567
00:23:31,559 --> 00:23:34,279
how much do you need for your bridal workshop?

568
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:42,839
80,000.

569
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:09,680
Sai Xiuli.

570
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,359
Think you're all grown up now, huh?

571
00:24:12,599 --> 00:24:13,599
Playing games, skipping class...

572
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,119
Did we send you to school...

573
00:24:15,359 --> 00:24:16,599
...just to play games and skip class?

574
00:24:17,519 --> 00:24:18,680
I broke my back raising you...

575
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:20,160
just for you to play games and skip class?

576
00:24:20,519 --> 00:24:22,160
What on earth are you doing, Sai Xiuli?

577
00:24:23,079 --> 00:24:23,480
Sister-in-law...

578
00:24:24,079 --> 00:24:25,240
Did Dad yell at you?

579
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:33,880
Sister-in-law...

580
00:24:34,319 --> 00:24:35,960
Did Dad chew you out again when he got back?

581
00:24:36,799 --> 00:24:37,920
I didn't mean it like that.

582
00:24:39,039 --> 00:24:41,319
Dad... he probably misunderstood.

583
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:43,559
If he said anything to you,

584
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,359
please don't take it to heart.

585
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:46,240
You know how...

586
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,039
...Dad is.

587
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:50,079
He can be really harsh sometimes.

588
00:24:53,559 --> 00:24:54,640
Tired of cafeteria food, aren't you?

589
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:56,920
What do you want to eat this weekend?

590
00:24:59,440 --> 00:24:59,759
Xiuli,

591
00:25:00,839 --> 00:25:02,000
I know you're sensible,

592
00:25:02,359 --> 00:25:04,200
but you're a high school senior now.

593
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:06,319
Your top priority is to focus on studying.

594
00:25:06,319 --> 00:25:07,480
You need to get into a good university.

595
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:08,880
Only then will you do right by me.

596
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:09,599
You know that?

597
00:25:13,319 --> 00:25:14,039
Time for class.

598
00:25:14,559 --> 00:25:15,279
Eat well,

599
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,240
sleep well,

600
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:18,279
and no more staying up late.

601
00:25:18,599 --> 00:25:18,839
Just...

602
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:20,319
study hard, okay?

603
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:22,599
I'm hanging up.

604
00:25:34,599 --> 00:25:35,559
The auspicious hour is here!

605
00:25:35,559 --> 00:25:36,559
Fortune! Fortune! Fortune!

606
00:25:36,759 --> 00:25:39,039
Firecrackers roar, bringing gold galore!

607
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:39,799
Light the firecrackers!

608
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:48,160
Grand opening! Great, great!

609
00:25:50,559 --> 00:25:51,079
Leave it to you!

610
00:25:52,079 --> 00:25:53,799
Brothers, sisters, and neighbors!

611
00:25:53,799 --> 00:25:54,839
Let me introduce you to...

612
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:56,279
Laibu Real Estate!

613
00:25:56,359 --> 00:25:57,640
Laibu Real Estate!

614
00:25:57,720 --> 00:25:59,119
What services do we offer?

615
00:25:59,279 --> 00:26:00,279
Housing consultations,

616
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:01,279
buying and selling,

617
00:26:01,279 --> 00:26:02,200
buying and selling,

618
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:02,880
property rentals,

619
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:03,720
property registrations,

620
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:04,839
and property management!

621
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:06,680
Anything related to housing,

622
00:26:06,839 --> 00:26:08,519
we take care of it all!

623
00:26:08,519 --> 00:26:09,480
You—you handle everything?

624
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:10,400
School district homes:

625
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:11,880
Zhongfangyuan New District,

626
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:13,200
Sunshine Garden,

627
00:26:13,519 --> 00:26:15,279
elementary: First Experimental!

628
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:16,880
Laibu Real Estate!

629
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,720
Anything related to housing,

630
00:26:18,799 --> 00:26:20,519
we take care of it all!

631
00:26:21,319 --> 00:26:23,519
The zoned school is First Experimental,

632
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:24,839
Huayu High School,

633
00:26:25,079 --> 00:26:26,319
Dongyi Residence,

634
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:28,119
and a commercial apartment—

635
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:28,759
What?

636
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:29,319
Hold on.

637
00:26:29,559 --> 00:26:30,000
I'm busy here!

638
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:32,160
Hongdu Garden, commercial—

639
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:33,799
What is this place called?

640
00:26:35,519 --> 00:26:36,839
Laibu Real Estate.

641
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:38,920
So you know it's called Laibu Real Estate!

642
00:26:45,519 --> 00:26:46,839
Don't get cocky over a little sunshine,

643
00:26:46,839 --> 00:26:48,039
or run wild with a splash of water.

644
00:26:48,039 --> 00:26:48,880
I'm helping you out!

645
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:49,640
Stop running your mouth here.

646
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:50,119
Go dance!

647
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:53,960
Uh...

648
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:55,960
Anyway, if anyone needs, you know,

649
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:57,039
rentals or purchases,

650
00:26:57,039 --> 00:26:58,279
just—just come on over!

651
00:26:58,759 --> 00:26:59,960
Move up front!

652
00:27:00,519 --> 00:27:02,039
Take it seriously, dance properly!

653
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:05,359
Even if you don't need anything, drop by for tea!

654
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:06,720
Thank you, everyone!

655
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:07,559
You're all so enthusiastic!

656
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,160
I won't say much more.

657
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,599
I'll hand out red envelopes to everyone!

658
00:27:12,160 --> 00:27:13,119
Brothers, thanks for the hard work!

659
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:14,079
Just a little something, a token!

660
00:27:14,079 --> 00:27:15,240
Thank you, Boss! Thank you, Boss!

661
00:27:15,759 --> 00:27:17,200
Buy some smokes, have some drinks!

662
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:17,720
Just a small token!

663
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:18,200
Thanks for the red envelope, Boss Ma!

664
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:18,599
Don't mention it!

665
00:27:18,599 --> 00:27:18,960
Thank you, Boss!

666
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:19,480
Laibu.

667
00:27:19,599 --> 00:27:20,039
Thank you, Boss!

668
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,079
Quite lively.

669
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:21,799
Auntie!

670
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:22,680
It's my grand opening,

671
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:23,440
and you made a special trip!

672
00:27:24,079 --> 00:27:25,559
Auntie, I'm genuinely touched, really.

673
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,200
What's that saying again? Uh...

674
00:27:27,599 --> 00:27:29,759
"It gr-graces my humble abode," right?

675
00:27:29,759 --> 00:27:30,599
Where's the apartment you found for me?

676
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:32,640
Got it.

677
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:33,880
Of course I've got it!

678
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:34,720
Auntie, give me a second.

679
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:35,880
Kevin!

680
00:27:36,359 --> 00:27:37,200
Hurry, find the listing!

681
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:38,119
Right on it!

682
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,599
Where's—where's my binder? Hurry!

683
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:40,920
Auntie,

684
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:42,680
I've got a great apartment here.

685
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:44,319
Huatai Mansion.

686
00:27:47,319 --> 00:27:48,359
The best development right now.

687
00:27:48,559 --> 00:27:49,160
It's completely sold out.

688
00:27:49,599 --> 00:27:50,680
Only one model unit left.

689
00:27:51,079 --> 00:27:51,799
Move-in ready.

690
00:27:52,359 --> 00:27:53,039
You know that location.

691
00:27:53,319 --> 00:27:54,279
It's not far from where you work,

692
00:27:54,279 --> 00:27:55,400
or Uncle Ma's hospital.

693
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:56,039
What?

694
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:58,119
Want to make an agency fee off me too?

695
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,480
Reselling at cost.

696
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:00,880
Not making a single penny.

697
00:28:01,799 --> 00:28:02,440
Working for free.

698
00:28:02,839 --> 00:28:03,720
I'd like to make money too,

699
00:28:04,039 --> 00:28:04,759
but what can I do?

700
00:28:05,359 --> 00:28:06,359
You're Ma Laibu's aunt.

701
00:28:06,599 --> 00:28:07,599
With family like this,

702
00:28:07,599 --> 00:28:08,519
and he and I are like brothers.

703
00:28:08,799 --> 00:28:09,480
6,000 per square meter.

704
00:28:09,799 --> 00:28:10,279
60 square meters.

705
00:28:10,759 --> 00:28:11,240
360,000.

706
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:13,880
What's it called?

707
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:15,400
Huatai Mansion.

708
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:18,079
Laibu.

709
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:19,559
Let me see Huatai Mansion.

710
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:20,279
Hua—

711
00:28:21,079 --> 00:28:22,759
Auntie, great minds think alike!

712
00:28:23,519 --> 00:28:24,640
A one-bedroom at Huatai Mansion.

713
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:27,000
I get the cheapest units in the whole city.

714
00:28:27,559 --> 00:28:28,400
Cost is 7,000.

715
00:28:28,599 --> 00:28:29,359
I'll give it to you at cost.

716
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:30,240
Six times seven...

717
00:28:30,319 --> 00:28:31,279
Exactly 420,000.

718
00:28:31,799 --> 00:28:32,480
Ma Laibu!

719
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:34,759
You're ripping me off!

720
00:28:35,279 --> 00:28:36,759
You dare take money from me?

721
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:38,240
Come here, Sai Xiuhe. Tell him how much!

722
00:28:38,319 --> 00:28:38,559
Ow!

723
00:28:38,799 --> 00:28:39,200
Ma Laibu!

724
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:40,720
How much?

725
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:42,160
Isn't it 7,000?

726
00:28:42,279 --> 00:28:43,000
I quoted 6,000.

727
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:43,720
Wait, isn't 7,000 for regular customers?

728
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:45,039
This is how you look out for me, huh?

729
00:28:45,039 --> 00:28:46,480
Sai Xiuhe, you set me up, didn't you?

730
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:47,279
No, I didn't know!

731
00:28:47,279 --> 00:28:49,400
You're making money off your own family.

732
00:28:49,759 --> 00:28:50,319
Just you wait!

733
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:52,319
Let's go see the apartment.

734
00:28:52,559 --> 00:28:53,640
You really screwed me over, didn't you?

735
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:54,039
Boss Ma,

736
00:28:54,279 --> 00:28:56,079
I'm taking your aunt to see the place.

737
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:57,599
Just wait till you get back!

738
00:29:17,559 --> 00:29:18,119
Sleep a little longer.

739
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:19,839
I just worked a night shift.

740
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:24,839
Do you love me?

741
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:27,599
Yes, yes. So much.

742
00:29:28,039 --> 00:29:29,759
But I still want a baby.

743
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:34,599
Don't listen to people saying you must have a kid.

744
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:36,720
Who's gonna raise it?

745
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:38,680
But I really want one.

746
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:40,480
I'm just stating facts.

747
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:41,279
Your mom is gone,

748
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:42,079
and mine is gone too.

749
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,079
Right?

750
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,160
Once the baby is born,

751
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:46,039
nannies aren't reliable either.

752
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:47,920
You'll be the one slaving away.

753
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,599
Come on, don't be mad. Don't be mad.

754
00:29:58,920 --> 00:29:59,920
Why even have a kid?

755
00:30:00,519 --> 00:30:02,039
All my friends say

756
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:04,759
a marriage without kids won't last.

757
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:07,119
I don't want us to split up.

758
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:09,319
We won't.

759
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,720
What kind of friends are they,

760
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,400
pushing you into misery like that?

761
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:14,400
Let me tell you,

762
00:30:14,759 --> 00:30:15,799
even if people have kids,

763
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:17,319
their whole lives just revolve around them.

764
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:19,160
There's zero quality of life.

765
00:30:20,599 --> 00:30:21,960
So you just don't want kids.

766
00:30:27,039 --> 00:30:27,960
My dearest wife,

767
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:29,599
I'm a doctor.

768
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,920
Let me explain from a medical perspective.

769
00:30:33,839 --> 00:30:36,319
Your mom had heart disease and diabetes,

770
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:37,119
plus asthma.

771
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:38,519
And your dad,

772
00:30:38,839 --> 00:30:39,480
high blood pressure,

773
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:40,599
and...

774
00:30:43,759 --> 00:30:44,279
Anyway,

775
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:46,599
checkups reveal tons of issues in old age.

776
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,279
So with our genetics,

777
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:51,039
there's really no need to pass them down.

778
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:04,920
Are you still coming over tonight?

779
00:31:12,359 --> 00:31:12,720
Never mind.

780
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:13,519
Go to sleep.

781
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:25,759
This is the rough

782
00:31:25,759 --> 00:31:27,039
interview outline we've put together.

783
00:31:27,039 --> 00:31:27,440
Right here.

784
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:28,759
Take a look and see if there are any issues.

785
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,119
What we did yesterday is fine.

786
00:31:31,119 --> 00:31:31,440
All right.

787
00:31:32,119 --> 00:31:32,920
Nothing else for now.

788
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,240
Sister Meifan, your sister-in-law is here.

789
00:31:40,519 --> 00:31:41,519
Take a look through the rest as well.

790
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:49,559
Stay back! Don't come up!

791
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,559
What's going on? Coming here looking for me?

792
00:31:55,279 --> 00:31:55,680
Here.

793
00:31:56,119 --> 00:31:56,759
I bought it for you.

794
00:31:57,039 --> 00:31:57,759
I can't take this.

795
00:31:58,119 --> 00:31:59,000
It's way too valuable.

796
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:01,000
Only something like this is worthy of you.

797
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:04,079
I bought it specially for you, specially for you.

798
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:12,799
About what happened at Mid-Autumn Festival,

799
00:32:14,119 --> 00:32:16,359
I've been wanting to apologize to Xiuliang,

800
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,279
but I felt too ashamed

801
00:32:18,279 --> 00:32:19,519
to face him.

802
00:32:21,799 --> 00:32:22,960
I heard from Xiuhe

803
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:25,160
that you sold your place

804
00:32:25,599 --> 00:32:27,039
and are still staying in a hotel.

805
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,839
That makes me feel even worse.

806
00:32:30,359 --> 00:32:31,160
As for what happened,

807
00:32:31,880 --> 00:32:33,079
I was in the wrong.

808
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:34,599
I acted too hastily.

809
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:35,279
I really—

810
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:36,279
Move this chair away.

811
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:36,920
Okay.

812
00:32:37,119 --> 00:32:37,759
It's about to start.

813
00:32:37,759 --> 00:32:38,559
Why leave it here?

814
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:40,440
Meifan,

815
00:32:40,880 --> 00:32:42,480
please be the bigger person.

816
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:45,440
Don't take it to heart.

817
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:47,279
Let's just put it behind us.

818
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,240
I also heard that

819
00:32:49,559 --> 00:32:51,279
as long as Xiuliang goes back to work,

820
00:32:52,759 --> 00:32:54,359
Dad is willing to give you a share.

821
00:32:54,599 --> 00:32:55,519
Is that true?

822
00:32:55,799 --> 00:32:57,000
We appreciate Dad's good intentions,

823
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:59,480
but this isn't child's play

824
00:32:59,599 --> 00:33:00,400
where you can just quit on a whim.

825
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:01,960
As for Dad,

826
00:33:02,319 --> 00:33:02,880
I believe

827
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:05,039
we'll resolve this sooner or later.

828
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:05,839
Right.

829
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:07,640
Of course.

830
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,359
Fathers and sons share a bond.

831
00:33:09,799 --> 00:33:11,160
As long as Xiuliang asks,

832
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:12,359
Dad will give him anything.

833
00:33:16,079 --> 00:33:17,680
Still, out of that 14 million,

834
00:33:18,880 --> 00:33:20,359
how much do you plan to take?

835
00:33:22,359 --> 00:33:23,359
We don't want that money.

836
00:33:30,119 --> 00:33:30,640
Meifan.

837
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:32,039
Honestly,

838
00:33:32,599 --> 00:33:34,160
now that Dad wants to split the money,

839
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,759
I think it's a good thing.

840
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:37,440
The rest of us

841
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:39,480
shouldn't be fighting among ourselves.

842
00:33:40,079 --> 00:33:41,200
What I mean is,

843
00:33:41,559 --> 00:33:43,119
why don't you talk to Xiuliang,

844
00:33:43,119 --> 00:33:44,119
and we'll set up a time

845
00:33:44,759 --> 00:33:46,279
for all of us to sit down and talk?

846
00:33:46,279 --> 00:33:47,039
We can talk it through

847
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:49,079
and agree on a plan ourselves first.

848
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,559
See what everyone is thinking,

849
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,200
how much everyone wants,

850
00:33:54,039 --> 00:33:55,039
and what would be fair.

851
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:57,519
Let's lay it all out in the open.

852
00:33:57,960 --> 00:33:58,920
Once we work it out,

853
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:00,319
we can go to Dad together.

854
00:34:01,079 --> 00:34:03,039
That's better than Dad deciding on a whim,

855
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:04,680
only for us later

856
00:34:05,319 --> 00:34:05,599
to, you know,

857
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:08,079
have hard feelings about it.

858
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:08,800
Are you done?

859
00:34:10,960 --> 00:34:11,880
I get what you mean.

860
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:12,960
I'll pass it along.

861
00:34:18,239 --> 00:34:18,800
Go about your business.

862
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:19,880
Don't mind me.

863
00:34:21,239 --> 00:34:21,880
Go ahead and use it.

864
00:34:22,079 --> 00:34:22,880
It smells so good.

865
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:24,199
I tested it at the counter today.

866
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:27,360
Xiao Xu.

867
00:34:28,119 --> 00:34:28,840
Take this out to her.

868
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:29,119
Okay.

869
00:34:31,880 --> 00:34:32,800
I didn't steer you wrong, did I?

870
00:34:33,119 --> 00:34:33,599
It's all right.

871
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:34,400
Let me tell you,

872
00:34:34,599 --> 00:34:36,440
Ma the third wanted this listing too.

873
00:34:36,679 --> 00:34:37,559
They wouldn't give it to him.

874
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:39,000
He couldn't close the deal.

875
00:34:40,079 --> 00:34:41,119
Aren't you two always together?

876
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:42,880
Childhood friends or not,

877
00:34:43,199 --> 00:34:44,159
Auntie, not to brag,

878
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:46,199
he's done business with me since childhood.

879
00:34:46,599 --> 00:34:48,599
The first few contracts he closed,

880
00:34:48,599 --> 00:34:49,599
I negotiated them for him.

881
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:51,360
He always thought trading property

882
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:52,320
was just about the property.

883
00:34:52,719 --> 00:34:53,440
But it's not.

884
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:54,320
It's about people.

885
00:34:54,880 --> 00:34:55,599
It's about human nature.

886
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:57,000
You have to figure out first:

887
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,320
Why does the seller want to sell?

888
00:34:58,519 --> 00:34:59,519
Are they strapped for cash?

889
00:35:00,079 --> 00:35:00,920
And the buyer—

890
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:02,280
what do they see in the place?

891
00:35:02,559 --> 00:35:03,840
Is it the school district,

892
00:35:04,079 --> 00:35:05,199
or the good location?

893
00:35:05,599 --> 00:35:06,840
Are they going to live in it,

894
00:35:07,159 --> 00:35:08,920
or flip it to make a buck?

895
00:35:09,440 --> 00:35:10,719
Figure all that out,

896
00:35:10,719 --> 00:35:11,800
and only then can you make the sale.

897
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,199
He hasn't got a clue.

898
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,000
Since you know people so well,

899
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:16,559
giving me this house at such a price—

900
00:35:17,280 --> 00:35:17,679
what's your angle?

901
00:35:18,079 --> 00:35:19,119
Nothing at all.

902
00:35:19,199 --> 00:35:19,719
Cut the crap.

903
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:22,119
There's no free lunch in this world.

904
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:24,039
We've only met three times,

905
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:26,159
yet you show me a place late at night,

906
00:35:26,159 --> 00:35:27,000
without making a dime.

907
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:28,239
What,

908
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:31,519
do I look like your long-lost God of Wealth?

909
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:34,239
Well, you're way prettier than the God of Wealth.

910
00:35:34,719 --> 00:35:35,559
To be honest with you,

911
00:35:35,960 --> 00:35:36,679
the first time I saw you,

912
00:35:36,679 --> 00:35:38,480
I thought you were gorgeous and sharp,

913
00:35:38,679 --> 00:35:39,480
and very easy on the eyes.

914
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:40,360
What?

915
00:35:41,039 --> 00:35:41,639
Trying to hit on me?

916
00:35:44,639 --> 00:35:45,119
Can't I?

917
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:45,760
Sure.

918
00:35:47,519 --> 00:35:48,360
Then tell me,

919
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:49,599
what do you like about me?

920
00:35:50,639 --> 00:35:51,239
Tell the truth.

921
00:35:51,679 --> 00:35:52,239
If you don't,

922
00:35:52,239 --> 00:35:52,920
I'm walking right now.

923
00:35:55,119 --> 00:35:56,079
What I just said—

924
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:57,920
gorgeous, sharp, easy on the eyes—

925
00:35:58,360 --> 00:35:59,280
that was all true.

926
00:36:00,079 --> 00:36:00,599
But you know,

927
00:36:01,199 --> 00:36:02,480
aren't you in charge of loans?

928
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:04,239
Hook me up with some while you're at it.

929
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:08,960
I approve loans,

930
00:36:09,519 --> 00:36:10,400
I don't run a charity.

931
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:12,480
Loans require collateral.

932
00:36:12,719 --> 00:36:13,159
What do you have?

933
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:14,079
Me.

934
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:17,800
A handsome guy right here.

935
00:36:18,079 --> 00:36:18,360
Come on,

936
00:36:19,159 --> 00:36:19,679
give me an appraisal.

937
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:20,599
How much can I get?

938
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:21,719
Trying to use your looks

939
00:36:21,719 --> 00:36:22,960
to become a social climber and live-in son-in-law?

940
00:36:23,719 --> 00:36:24,400
Your scheming

941
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:25,960
is so loud I can hear it at the bank.

942
00:36:26,119 --> 00:36:27,639
Hey, that's a bit harsh.

943
00:36:28,440 --> 00:36:29,559
Making money isn't shameful.

944
00:36:30,079 --> 00:36:31,119
Letting Ma the third

945
00:36:31,119 --> 00:36:32,559
flaunt his petty demolition money

946
00:36:32,559 --> 00:36:33,360
and walk all over me,

947
00:36:33,360 --> 00:36:34,719
calling me "kid" every single day—

948
00:36:34,719 --> 00:36:35,320
now that's humiliating.

949
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:36,199
Got it.

950
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,599
You want to make your first fortune off me.

951
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:40,079
Sai Xiuhe,

952
00:36:40,800 --> 00:36:42,000
trying to get something for nothing...

953
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:42,920
You sure have some nerve.

954
00:36:44,039 --> 00:36:44,440
As for the loan,

955
00:36:45,119 --> 00:36:46,079
I really do want it.

956
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:47,679
And as for you,

957
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:49,639
I really do want to pursue you.

958
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:50,360
How about it?

959
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:51,360
Honest enough.

960
00:36:52,039 --> 00:36:52,880
This place is nice.

961
00:36:53,199 --> 00:36:53,639
I'll take it.

962
00:36:55,679 --> 00:36:56,320
What about me?

963
00:36:56,719 --> 00:36:57,199
Do you want me?

964
00:36:57,519 --> 00:36:58,480
Think about it, please?

965
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:02,079
Wait till I get there.

966
00:37:03,159 --> 00:37:04,199
Go ahead and eat first.

967
00:37:05,039 --> 00:37:06,280
Don't drink iced Coke.

968
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:07,440
Jiaqi,

969
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:08,480
sweetheart,

970
00:37:08,480 --> 00:37:09,559
do you need me to bring you anything else?

971
00:37:09,559 --> 00:37:10,599
Are you home?

972
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:12,480
I'm here, I'm here. On a call.

973
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:14,440
I bought some pretty clothes.

974
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:15,800
Let me show you.

975
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:17,119
Go ahead, tell me.

976
00:37:17,119 --> 00:37:17,559
Look at this.

977
00:37:18,519 --> 00:37:19,000
Go ahead.

978
00:37:22,199 --> 00:37:23,599
I'll take it off and show you right now.

979
00:37:26,480 --> 00:37:27,480
All right, all right, I got it.

980
00:37:27,480 --> 00:37:28,199
Okay, okay, okay.

981
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:30,280
Yeah, yeah, sure.

982
00:37:52,679 --> 00:37:53,079
Honey,

983
00:37:54,199 --> 00:37:55,440
something urgent came up at the hospital.

984
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:56,400
I have to run over.

985
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:57,559
I'll be right back.

986
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:58,639
Go ahead and try on your clothes.

987
00:37:59,039 --> 00:38:00,159
I'll admire them properly when I get back.

988
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:06,719
My wife is so gorgeous,

989
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:07,920
you look great in whatever you wear.

990
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:09,480
I'll be back in no time.

991
00:38:36,639 --> 00:38:37,480
Today Wen Jiayin

992
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:38,920
actually came looking for me at the TV station.

993
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:40,880
She asked if we wanted to split the money.

994
00:38:41,199 --> 00:38:42,000
I said we're not splitting it.

995
00:38:42,559 --> 00:38:43,559
Then she said,

996
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:44,800
"In that case,

997
00:38:45,679 --> 00:38:47,360
let Xiuliang organize things,

998
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:48,559
to see how this money

999
00:38:48,559 --> 00:38:49,480
should be split among everyone."

1000
00:38:54,239 --> 00:38:55,280
So from what you're saying,

1001
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:58,320
she's trying to use me as a pawn,

1002
00:38:58,960 --> 00:39:00,239
using my name to split the money.

1003
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,199
Didn't she say earlier we wouldn't split it?

1004
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:44,119
Xiuliang, I'm busy.

1005
00:39:44,119 --> 00:39:44,679
Let me ask you this.

1006
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:46,840
You went to see Meifan today?

1007
00:39:49,719 --> 00:39:50,880
I... I went to see Meifan today,

1008
00:39:51,079 --> 00:39:53,199
and bought her a great cosmetics set.

1009
00:39:53,719 --> 00:39:54,159
Hold on.

1010
00:39:54,639 --> 00:39:54,960
Stop right there.

1011
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:56,800
If I'm not mistaken,

1012
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,440
what you wanted

1013
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:01,320
was to probe her to see

1014
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:03,119
what the second Sai brother is thinking,

1015
00:40:03,599 --> 00:40:05,039
and if he wants a cut of the family money.

1016
00:40:05,119 --> 00:40:05,719
Isn't that it?

1017
00:40:08,519 --> 00:40:09,840
You should've just said so.

1018
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:12,400
Why beat around the bush?

1019
00:40:12,760 --> 00:40:13,360
Here's what you do.

1020
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:14,559
Call the eldest,

1021
00:40:15,039 --> 00:40:15,400
the third,

1022
00:40:15,760 --> 00:40:16,880
the fourth, and the fifth.

1023
00:40:17,119 --> 00:40:17,719
Let's find a place

1024
00:40:17,719 --> 00:40:19,000
to talk it through face-to-face.

1025
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,440
Put everything on the table.

1026
00:40:20,440 --> 00:40:21,360
No holding back.

1027
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:22,239
How does that sound?

1028
00:40:24,039 --> 00:40:24,440
Fine.

1029
00:40:25,559 --> 00:40:25,840
All right.

1030
00:40:28,679 --> 00:40:29,159
Dealing with her

1031
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:30,559
takes the most direct approach.

1032
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:31,639
Leave it to you.

1033
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:45,679
Who is it?

1034
00:40:51,920 --> 00:40:52,519
I'm busy.

1035
00:40:55,239 --> 00:40:56,079
What do you want with me?

1036
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:58,880
Give Qianjin a call.

1037
00:41:00,119 --> 00:41:01,320
Why would I call her?

1038
00:41:01,679 --> 00:41:02,400
To talk.

1039
00:41:03,079 --> 00:41:03,800
Talk about what?

1040
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:06,519
Look.

1041
00:41:07,199 --> 00:41:07,920
Your eldest brother,

1042
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:08,760
me,

1043
00:41:09,239 --> 00:41:10,280
your second brother and his wife,

1044
00:41:10,599 --> 00:41:12,280
you, Qianjin, and Xiao Wu...

1045
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:13,880
We should all sit down together

1046
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:15,440
and talk this through,

1047
00:41:15,840 --> 00:41:16,679
to figure out the family money

1048
00:41:16,679 --> 00:41:17,360
and how to split it.

1049
00:41:18,159 --> 00:41:19,639
No petty schemes from anyone this time.

1050
00:41:20,079 --> 00:41:21,280
Put everything on the table,

1051
00:41:22,119 --> 00:41:22,880
totally open and honest.

1052
00:41:25,039 --> 00:41:25,559
Wen Jiayin,

1053
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:28,679
do you think I, Sai Xiuhe, am an idiot?

1054
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:30,320
How many times have you screwed me over?

1055
00:41:31,639 --> 00:41:32,960
You think I can trust you this time?

1056
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:38,119
I swear on your eldest brother's career.

1057
00:41:38,679 --> 00:41:40,320
No backing out, no dirty tricks.

1058
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:42,239
If I back out,

1059
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:43,159
Strike me dead.

1060
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:44,639
You won't even have to deal with me.

1061
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:49,559
I swear.

1062
00:42:20,760 --> 00:42:21,199
What is it?

1063
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:22,960
Lao Si, what are you up to?

1064
00:42:23,400 --> 00:42:24,159
Got some time in the next couple of days?

1065
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:25,639
What do you want? Just spit it out.

1066
00:42:26,039 --> 00:42:26,559
What do you mean, "what"?

1067
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:27,199
To talk.

1068
00:42:27,719 --> 00:42:28,119
About what?

1069
00:42:28,400 --> 00:42:29,639
About how to split the estate.

1070
00:42:29,639 --> 00:42:30,599
About how to split the money.

1071
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:31,639
What's that got to do with me?

1072
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:20,480
Dad,

1073
00:43:21,519 --> 00:43:22,480
take care of yourself,

1074
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:24,920
and hold this family together.

1075
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:27,960
We can't end up like the Mas.

1076
00:43:28,360 --> 00:43:30,480
Are you hiding something from me?

1077
00:43:30,920 --> 00:43:32,760
Dad loves you the most.

1078
00:43:33,400 --> 00:43:36,280
You can't team up with them to lie to me.

1079
00:43:36,519 --> 00:43:37,079
In this family,

1080
00:43:37,079 --> 00:43:38,400
am I really that useless?

1081
00:43:38,639 --> 00:43:39,599
What kind of big brother am I?

1082
00:43:39,599 --> 00:43:40,440
What kind of big brother am I?

1083
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:41,400
Then what does that make me?

1084
00:43:41,719 --> 00:43:42,679
I'm nothing at all!

1085
00:43:42,679 --> 00:43:43,840
I can't do anything right!

1086
00:43:44,159 --> 00:43:45,719
I'm the bad guy no matter what! I...
